<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose four points to 1,266.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose four points to 1,266.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,266 today from 1,262 on June 12, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1334    12.113	  1322    12.006</p>
<p>   1a   1265  9581.000	  1258  9525.000</p>
<p>   2    1494    21.344	  1484    21.206</p>
<p>   2a   1418 11631.000	  1406 11531.000</p>
<p>   3    1324    12.219	  1318    12.163</p>
<p>   3a   1170  9231.000	  1152  9094.000</p>
